{"repositoryId":664072814,"availability":"available","full":"KIRTISINHA11/Linkedin-Personalized-Post-Recommender-System","name":"Linkedin-Personalized-Post-Recommender-System","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2023-07-08T20:56:17Z","updated":"2026-10-17T13:17:54Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kirtibert.streamlit.app/","topics":[],"demo":"https://kirtibert.streamlit.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T18:18:57.568Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T18:18:57.568Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T18:18:57.568Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T18:18:57.568Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["🤖 An autonomous, multi-agent LinkedIn content system — built on top of my own published NLP research.","This repository began as a research project (see legacy-research-prototype/) comparing BERT, GPT-2, and classical ML for content-based LinkedIn post recommendation (published at ICCCNT'2023). It has since grown into a full agentic AI pipeline: an autonomous system that selects topics, recommends related existing content using the paper's own BERT-similarity method, researches facts in real time, drafts original LinkedIn posts, validates them with an independent LLM guardrail, checks semantic uniqueness, and (optionally) publishes on a schedule — all orchestrated as a stateful LangGraph…","Status: Fully functional in dry-run mode end-to-end (topic selection → recommendation → research → generation → validation → duplicate detection). Live LinkedIn publishing is implemented and tested against the real API but kept as a deliberate next step — see Publishing to LinkedIn."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/KIRTISINHA11/Linkedin-Personalized-Post-Recommender-System/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d0ff6bc08704d7addc708c51b5b51c298660e75f9933a5db29080fd194540aa1","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T